          <td><span class="postbody">First, blame me. I threw out Mistmoore expecting it to not be hugely populated, but I ended up picking the busiest server on the farm. Figures.
<br />

<br />
With that said, Mistmoore has gotten, even midday (3pmish) to a Full state. For those of us who lived through Xegony, we know how much of a pain in the ass that is and how it boggs the server down.
<br />

<br />
After talking to folks, most agree it's best to change servers to one of the ones that just came up new since we are all still very low levels and it will just take a couple hours to get back to where we were.
<br />

<br />
So, with that said, we are remaking on Nektulos. The server is listed as light currently and was just brought online yesterday so it missed the first day rush.
<br />

<br />
Still going evil for main guys, so post your character names on this thread and I will update this and remove the other.
<br />

<br />
I don't think we have a ton of time into it and considering that most weren't in beta, the island was mostly a learning experience into the game anyway and can be knocked out fairly fast.
<br />

<br />
With that said, if you can, stay on the island long enough to buy all the crafting books if you can. They were more expensive in the city based upon what my brother has told me. Might be something to check with your mains before you remake though.
<br />

<br />
I hope you all decide to remake and join us. Obviously that is a choice you all will need to make, but I hope to see you there. Again, sorry, but I think overall it will be far better for all of us so we can make sure everyone can play together.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Thank you for your understanding,
<br />

<br />
The Management.
<br />

<br />
PS. Remember, Thursday is clean out the fridge day. Be sure to get rid of the stuff you don't want before then or it goes into the trash.<span style="color: red"></span><span style="color: red"></span><span style="color: red"></span></span><span class="gensmall"><i><br /><br />Last edited by Carstman on Wed Nov 10, 2004 4:50 pm; edited 2 times in total</i></span></td>
